  "question": {
    "text": "Moment of inertia of a body about a given axis is <math><mn>1.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Initially the body is at rest. In order to produce a rotational kinetic energy of <math><mn>1200</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the angular acceleration of <math><mn>20</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> must be applied about the axis for a duration of:"
